  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "",
    "constraints": [
      "Chef has received a mathematics assignment that requires array transformations.",
      "Given an array AAA of size NNN and a positive integer MMM, perform these steps:",
      "First, create array BBB such that Bi=Ai×M!&nbsp;;B_i = A_i \\times M!\\ ;Bi​=Ai​×M!&nbsp;; (M!(M!(M! denotes the factorial of M)M)M).",
      "Then, for each element in array BBB, calculate F(Bi)F(B_i)F(Bi​), where F(x)F(x)F(x) represents the number of divisors of xxx.",
      "Since these values can be large, output each F(Bi)F(B_i)F(Bi​) modulo (109+7)(10^9 + 7)(109+7).",
      "Input Format",
      "The first line of input contains two space-separated integers NNN and MMM, as mentioned in the statement.",
      "The second line of input contains NNN space-separated integers, denoting the elements of array AAA .",
      "Output Format",
      "Output NNN space-separated integers representing F(Bi)F(B_i)F(Bi​) modulo (109+7)(10^9 + 7)(109+7).",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105.",
      "1≤M≤1001 \\leq M \\leq 1001≤M≤100.",
      "1≤Ai≤1051 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^51≤Ai​≤105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3 3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "4 6 6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe initial array A=[1,2,3]A = [1, 2, 3]A=[1,2,3] and M=3M = 3M=3. Thus M!=3⋅2⋅1=6M! = 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 = 6M!=3⋅2⋅1=6.\nThe array B=[1⋅6,2⋅6,3⋅6]=[6,12,18]B = [1\\cdot 6, 2\\cdot 6, 3\\cdot 6] = [6, 12, 18]B=[1⋅6,2⋅6,3⋅6]=[6,12,18].\nThe number of divisors of 6,12,6, 12,6,12, and 181818 are 4,6,4, 6,4,6, and 666 respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
